Package: rts2-python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: rts2-db
Description: Remote Telescope System 2 - Python client scripting support
 RTS2 (Remote Telescope System, 2nd version) is a distributed control
 system for robotic astronomical observatories.
 .
 This package contains the rts2 Python module RTS2's "exe" observation
 scripts import: rts2.scriptcomm, the library they use to talk to the
 running system (device values, state, exposures, image handling, ...),
 rts2.flats, the sky-flat engine that a site's per-camera flat
 scripts configure and drive, and rts2.grb_query, which reads GRB details
 for a target out of the RTS2 database, together with the site-independent
 scripts (focus.py, vaodscan.py) in /usr/share/rts2/scripts.
 .
 Scripts specific to one observatory are not packaged. Each site keeps its
 own in /etc/rts2/scripts, a directory or a symlink to a checkout of them.
 rts2-base's script-path resolution ([scriptexec] script_path in rts2.ini,
 default /etc/rts2/scripts:/usr/share/rts2/scripts) finds a script by bare
 filename, e.g. "exe guideccd.py", the site's directory first. Pure Python,
 no compiled extensions; the same setup.py this package builds from is
 also directly pip-installable.
